     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · BBC Science · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>£6M Lottery Grant Awarded to Restore Scottish Atlantic Rainforest</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A five-year project titled 'Our Rainforest Futures' has secured nearly £6 million from the National Lottery Heritage Fund to restore Scotland’s rare Atlantic rainforest. Led by the Woodland Trust Scotland, the initiative will establish conservation hubs in Torridon, Morvern, and mid-Argyll to train locals in deer management and invasive species removal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/6m-lottery-grant-awarded-to-restore-scottish-atlantic-rainfo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Covering 75,000 acres, the rainforest faces threats from overgrazing and disease. The project aims to create over 20 jobs and 15 trainee posts to protect the unique habitat, which supports rare species like glow worms and lichens. Organizers hope to boost public awareness, as recent surveys show most people remain unaware of the region's ecological significance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and well-structured, capturing the project's scope, funding, and goals effectively.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn8w8n5ynq2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Science</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
