     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Akhilesh Yadav Defends Ayodhya Visit Amid Political Criticism</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samajwadi Party leader Akhilesh Yadav announced a December 12 visit to the Ram Temple in Ayodhya, asserting that &quot;God belongs to everyone&quot; despite BJP allegations of political motivation. Yadav criticized the BJP's governance, citing high unemployment and inflation, and claimed voters are prepared to elect his party in 2027.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/akhilesh-yadav-defends-ayodhya-visit-amid-political-criticis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During a press briefing in Lucknow, Yadav accused the BJP of electoral fraud and urged party workers to secure booths. He also demanded that voter lists be linked to biometric Aadhaar cards to prevent the creation of fake entries, framing the measure as a necessary step for digital accountability.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the political context and policy demands mentioned in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/uttar-pradesh/god-belongs-to-everyone-says-akhilesh-on-his-ayodhya-visit/article71690329.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/ayodhya/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ayodhya</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
