     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Anthropic Founders to Cash Out Millions in Anticipated IPO</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Anthropic</span> <span>#IPO</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#TechCrunch</span></div>
       <p>As Anthropic moves towards an initial public offering (IPO) that could value the company at $1.4 trillion, its S-1 filing has revealed details about the share sales planned by its seven co-founders. Each founder intends to sell an identical number of shares.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/anthropic-founders-to-cash-out-millions-in-anticipated-ipo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Specifically, each of the seven co-founders will sell 3,378,378 shares. With Anthropic floating an initial price range of $70 to $78 per share, the midpoint price of $74 would see each founder take in just shy of $250 million. At the low end of $70, each would pocket over $236 million, while the high end of $78 would yield just under $264 million. The S-1 filing also hints at strong demand, with board member Reed Hastings indicating a desire to purchase $300 million worth of shares and Christopher Liddell planning to buy $3 million.</p><p>The seven co-founders include CEO Dario Amodei, President and Chair of the Board Daniela Amodei, Chief Compute Officer Tom Brown, Head of Public Benefit Jack Clark, Chief Science Officer Jared Kaplan, Chief Architect Sam McCandlish, and Interpretability Research Lead Christopher Olah.</p><p>Following these sales, each founder will own approximately 3.2% of the total outstanding Class A shares, cumulatively holding around 22%. While other holders, such as Amazon and Google, possess nonvoting Class N shares, the founders collectively retain control of the company. Each founder will also receive one share of Class F stock, which carries supervoting rights, ensuring the group controls 51.1% of the votes, with no single founder holding significantly more shares or votes than others.</p><p>The genesis of Anthropic traces back to 2021 when its founders departed OpenAI due to disagreements over the approach to building AI. Siblings Dario and Daniela Amodei, who held senior research and policy roles at OpenAI, joined five former colleagues to establish a company that has publicly emphasized a greater focus on AI safety compared to its rivals, including their previous employer.</p><p>What to watch: The final IPO pricing and market reception for Anthropic.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft provides a comprehensive and accurate summary of the S-1 filing details and background information provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/10/all-7-anthropic-founders-will-each-cash-out-about-250m-in-ipo/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
