     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Assam CM Supports Paternity Case Against Harak Singh Rawat</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Assam Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma has publicly backed Indira Dewri, who alleges she was raped and impregnated by former Uttarakhand Minister Harak Singh Rawat in 2003. Dewri is demanding a fresh CBI probe and a DNA test to establish the paternity of her 23-year-old son, claiming previous investigations were insufficient.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/assam-cm-supports-paternity-case-against-harak-singh-rawat.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rawat has denied all allegations, labeling them politically motivated by the BJP ahead of the 2027 state elections. While a prior court-supervised DNA test reportedly showed no match, Dewri insists on new testing and protection, citing threats. She is currently in Dehradun seeking justice from Uttarakhand leadership.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the paternity dispute and the political tension surrounding the case.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/assam/assam-cm-himanta-sarma-backs-womans-paternity-case-against-ex-uttarakhand-minister/article71689693.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
