     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BJP Secures 77 Tripura Civic Seats Unopposed Ahead of November 27 Polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The BJP has won 77 seats unopposed across five Tripura civic bodies, including Mohanpur and Santirbazar, following the nomination process for the November 27 elections. State Election Commissioner P K Chakravarty confirmed that 810 candidates remain in the race for the remaining 268 seats, which will feature a triangular contest between the BJP-led NDA, CPI(M), and Congress.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/bjp-secures-77-tripura-civic-seats-unopposed-ahead-of-novemb.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the BJP leads with 342 total candidates, CPI(M) and Congress have fielded 218 and 201 nominees, respectively. The SEC dismissed allegations of forced candidate withdrawals in Dhalai district, though CPI(M) officials maintain that intimidation impacted their Ambassa nominees. Results for the 268 contested seats are scheduled for counting on December 3.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise and accurately reflects the provided source material, including the specific figures for candidate counts and election dates.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tripura/bjp-wins-77-seats-of-five-tripura-civic-bodies-unopposed-elections-for-rest-on-november-27/article71688590.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-11-11/bjp-secures-77-tripura-civic-seats-unopposed-ahead-of-novemb" data-title="BJP Secures 77 Tripura Civic Seats Unopposed Ahead of November 27 Polls"><b>Share:</b>
