     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-11-11 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Centre Extends Medical Device PLI Scheme to 2036, Eases Entry Barriers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health Policy</span> <span>#Medical Devices</span> <span>#PLI Scheme</span> <span>#Government Incentives</span></div>
       <p>The Centre has extended the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for medical devices until 2036, according to new guidelines. This extension aims to ease entry barriers for participants in the sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/centre-extends-medical-device-pli-scheme-to-2036-eases-entry.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Under the revised framework, the minimum sales threshold requirement for claiming incentives has been discontinued. Additionally, the minimum investment requirement has been trimmed to make the scheme more attractive and investor-friendly.</p><p>These changes are designed to foster greater participation and investment in the domestic medical device manufacturing industry.</p><p>What to watch: Impact on domestic medical device manufacturing and new investor interest.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft covers the primary changes from the source summary. It is thin, but the source material provided was very limited.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/policy/centre-extends-medical-device-pli-scheme-to-2036-invites-fresh-applications/135723201" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
