     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CII Partnership Summit 2026 Begins in Visakhapatnam with Global Participation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#CII Summit</span> <span>#Visakhapatnam</span> <span>#Economic Forum</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>The 31st CII Partnership Summit 2026 commenced on Thursday, November 12, 2026, in Visakhapatnam. Jointly organized by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Government of India, the Government of Andhra Pradesh, and the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII), the two-day global economic forum is themed “Navigating Change: Technology, Trust and Trade – Leading the Way in a New World Order”. Union Minister for Home Affairs and Cooperation Amit Shah is scheduled to address the inaugural session.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/cii-partnership-summit-2026-begins-in-visakhapatnam-with-glo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Over 3,800 delegates, including senior policymakers, 15 international ministers, and global corporate executives from nearly 59 countries, are expected to participate. Union Minister for Commerce and Industry Piyush Goyal will chair the summit deliberations, while Vice-President of India C.P. Radhakrishnan and Governor S. Abdul Nazeer will attend the valedictory session. Andhra Pradesh Chief Minister N. Chandrababu Naidu will co-chair, focusing on state-level economic initiatives, with Minister for IT, Electronics and Communications Nara Lokesh engaging in technology dialogues.</p><p>The summit will feature an overseas ministerial and diplomatic presence from countries such as Singapore, the United Arab Emirates, the Slovak Republic, and Guatemala. Notable international delegates include Japan's Ambassador to India Keiichi Ono and Russia's Ambassador to India Denis Alipov. Organisations like the Asian Development Bank and the United Nations Environment Programme are also attending. Corporate leaders such as ReNew Chairman Sumant Sinha and CII Vice-President Shashwat Goenka will lead core thematic tracks.</p><p>Deliberations are structured across six core tracks: global trade and investment, geoeconomics, talent and mobility, clean energy, technology, and agriculture. Organizers anticipate the signing of over 160 Memoranda of Understanding and Government Orders during the forum. Chief Secretary G. Sai Prasad will highlight Andhra Pradesh's ease of doing business and investment climate.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive summary of the summit details, participants, and structure. Effectively captures the scope of the event using the provided source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/cii-partnership-summit-begins-in-visakhapatnam-on-november-12-amit-shah-to-address-inaugural-session/article71688259.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/visakhapatnam/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visakhapatnam</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
