     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>EPFO Enables Digital Life Certificate Submission via UMANG App</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Employees' Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) has launched an online facility for EPS-95 pensioners to generate and submit their Digital Life Certificate (Jeevan Pramaan) from home. Pensioners can use the UMANG app and Aadhaar-based face authentication to renew their certificates annually, avoiding the need for physical submissions to banks or EPFO offices.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/epfo-enables-digital-life-certificate-submission-via-umang-a.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To complete the process, users must install the AadhaarFaceRD application and provide pension details within the UMANG app. Once face authentication is successful, the certificate is stored in the Jeevan Pramaan repository and made available electronically to the pension disbursing agency. This digital system ensures uninterrupted pension payments without requiring in-person visits.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and effectively summarizes the process for submitting a Digital Life Certificate via the UMANG app as described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/eps95-pensioners-epfo-says-submit-digital-life-certificate-from-home-using-umang-app-heres-step-by-step-process-11794374496507.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
