     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Equity Mutual Fund Inflows Decline in October as Investors Favor Large-Caps</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Equity mutual fund inflows dropped 14% to ₹32,994 crore in October as small-cap and mid-cap investments fell by 29% and 38% respectively. Conversely, large-cap funds saw a 20% increase, reaching ₹1,032 crore in inflows as investors sought to rebalance portfolios amid shifting market performance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/equity-mutual-fund-inflows-decline-in-october-as-investors-f.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Benchmark indices Nifty 50 and BSE Sensex rose in October, while small and mid-cap segments declined. Systematic Investment Plan (SIP) contributions also saw a marginal dip to ₹32,162 crore. Experts suggest the shift toward large-caps reflects a move toward attractive valuations, though confidence in the long-term growth potential of smaller segments remains.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the financial data and expert commentary from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
