     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gujarat man arrested for daughter's murder</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A 50-year-old man, Kaushal Patel, was arrested in Gujarat’s Anand district for strangling his 21-year-old daughter, Sania Patel, on November 8. Police report the father killed her using a dupatta after a confrontation regarding her relationship with a man from a different community.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/gujarat-man-arrested-for-daughters-murder.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The accused initially attempted to disguise the death as suicide. However, a forensic autopsy at Khambhat Government Hospital confirmed ligature strangulation, leading to a police investigation. Patel subsequently confessed to the crime, citing his strong opposition to his daughter's inter-faith relationship. He has been charged under Section 103(1) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief concisely covers the crime, the motive, the forensic findings, and the legal charges.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/khambhat-honour-killing-father-strangles-daughter-over-relationship-3036875-2026-11-11?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
