     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>HDFC Bank Raises Lending Rates by 5-15 Bps, Affecting Loan EMIs</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#personal finance</span> <span>#banking</span> <span>#loans</span> <span>#MCLR</span></div>
       <p>HDFC Bank has increased its marginal cost of funds-based lending rates (MCLR) by 5-15 basis points across all seven tenures, effective from November 7. Following this revision, the bank's MCLR rates now range from 7.85% to 8.70%, up from the previous 7.75% to 8.55%. This adjustment comes nearly a month after the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) raised its policy repo rate by 25 basis points, from 5.25% to 5.50%, on October 7, 2026.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/hdfc-bank-raises-lending-rates-by-5-15-bps-affecting-loan-em.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>MCLR is an internal benchmark set by banks to determine minimum lending rates, as mandated by the RBI since April 2016, replacing the older base rate system for greater transparency. The latest hike by HDFC Bank is steeper for longer-duration tenures, with the six-month, one-year, two-year, and three-year MCLR each rising by 15 basis points. This move could increase borrowing costs for customers whose home loans, personal loans, auto loans, and other floating-rate borrowings are linked to the bank's MCLR.</p><p>However, the impact on borrowers is not necessarily immediate. The actual effect will depend on the specific benchmark linked to the loan, the applicable spread, and the interest rate reset date outlined in the loan agreement. For example, if a home loan is linked to the one-year MCLR, the revised rate would typically be passed on at the loan's next annual reset date. Depending on the loan terms, a higher interest rate could result in either an increase in the monthly EMI or an extension of the loan tenure.</p><p>What to watch: Borrowers should review their loan agreements for specific interest rate reset dates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately conveys all technical details from the source, including the rate changes, effective date, and the mechanism of MCLR.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/hdfc-bank-raises-mclr-by-5-15-bps-across-all-tenures-check-new-lending-rates-and-what-they-mean-for-your-loan-emis-11794396761391.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
