     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India's Meetei Secures Boxing Final Berth at Youth Olympics</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Youth Olympics</span> <span>#Boxing</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Lairenlakpam Ambekar Meetei</span></div>
       <p>Indian boxer Lairenlakpam Ambekar Meetei has advanced to the final of the men's 50kg boxing competition at the 2026 Summer Youth Olympics in Dakar. Meetei secured his spot by defeating Colombia's Izzon Jeffrey Galea Arevalo with a dominant 5-0 victory on points in their semifinal bout on Wednesday. Competing from the red corner, Meetei’s performance was unanimously judged superior, with all five judges scoring the bout 28-27, 28-27, 28-27, 29-26, and 28-27 in his favor.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/indias-meetei-secures-boxing-final-berth-at-youth-olympics.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Meetei's path to the final included earlier decisive victories. In the quarterfinals, he defeated Faye Cheikh Ibrahima Fall of Senegal with another 5-0 points decision. Prior to that, he assured India of a medal by advancing to the semifinals after defeating Namibia's Abraham Kalenga via a Referee Stops Contest (RSC) in Round 1 at 1:57. In the upcoming final, Meetei is set to face Kristian Jubani of Ireland, who similarly blanked Alan Jesus Ocampo Cano of Mexico 5-0 in the other semifinal.</p><p>This marks the second medal India has secured in the boxing competition at the Youth Olympics. Earlier, Gunjan also assured India of a medal by reaching the semifinals of the women's 48kg category. Gunjan defeated Mexico's Atena Sofia Juarez Calero 5-0 on points and had received a bye in the first round, advancing directly to the quarterfinals. Gunjan is slated to compete against Lilly Bassett of Great Britain in her semifinal bout, with a bronze medal guaranteed even if she does not progress further.</p><p>As of the morning session on Wednesday, November 11, India's overall medal tally at the 2026 Summer Youth Olympics stands at nine medals, comprising three silver and six bronze. These medals have been won across wrestling, boxing, and swimming disciplines.</p><p>What to watch: Meetei's final bout and Gunjan's semifinal match.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a faithful and comprehensive summary of the provided text, accurately reflecting all names, figures, and event details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/boxing/youth-olympics-indias-lairenlakpam-ambekar-meetei-storms-into-final-of-mens-50kg-boxing-12313600#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
