     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala High Court Sets November 24 Deadline for Mental Health Center Upgrades</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Kerala High Court has ordered the state government to ensure mental health centers in Thiruvananthapuram, Thrissur, and Kozhikode are fully stocked with adequate medicines and vehicles by November 24. The court insisted that official assurances must translate into immediate, tangible improvements for patient care.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/kerala-high-court-sets-november-24-deadline-for-mental-healt.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Advocate General requested more time to finalize staff appointments due to administrative changes in the Health and Family Welfare department, while reporting that construction of facility compound walls is progressing steadily. Earlier this year, the government renamed these centers as &quot;happiness and wellness centers&quot; to reduce the social stigma surrounding mental health.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the court's directives and the government's progress.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/kerala-high-court-orders-government-to-ready-adequate-medicines-vehicles-at-mental-health-centres-by-november-24/article71690314.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
