      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/science">science</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>New Water Budgeting Framework Highlights Agricultural Inequality</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Researchers from the Indian Institute of Science have developed a new water budgeting framework to address social inequalities in agricultural groundwater usage. Published in the Journal of Hydrology, the study introduces the 'blue water potential' (BWP) indicator to measure groundwater replenishment versus consumption by different farming groups.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/new-water-budgeting-framework-highlights-agricultural-inequa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Applying this to a village in Andhra Pradesh, the study reveals that wealthier farmers utilizing orchards consume significantly more groundwater than they replenish, creating a negative BWP. Conversely, poorer rain-fed farmers contribute positively to groundwater recharge. The research highlights a hidden interdependence where intensive agricultural systems rely on the sustainability practices of economically disadvantaged groups.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and correctly captures the study's core findings and implications.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-11-account-role-neglected-farmer-groups.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
