     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana Nears Rs. 400 Crore Club, Sets New Week One Record</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Box Office</span> <span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Indian Cinema</span></div>
       <p>The Ranbir Kapoor and Yash-led film Ramayana, directed by Nitesh Tiwari, is poised to become one of Indian Cinema's biggest blockbusters. After accumulating Rs. 326.07 crore in its first six days, the film maintained a strong box office hold on Wednesday, according to Bollywood Hungama. Early estimates indicate Ramayana collected between Rs. 53 crore and Rs. 55 crore on its seventh day, pushing its total collections to approximately Rs. 380 crore.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/ramayana-nears-rs-400-crore-club-sets-new-week-one-record.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The film is on track to achieve an extended first-week collection close to Rs. 420 crore. This figure would secure it the biggest ever week one total of all time, second only to Dhurandhar 2. The Wednesday collections benefited from the Bhai Dooj holiday, though a slight dip is anticipated on Thursday. Despite this, the film's strong hold is expected to keep it in contention for the Rs. 1000 crore club in Hindi cinema.</p><p>Ramayana continues to perform phenomenally in mass belts as the Diwali impact fades and the holiday period extends. Gujarat, in particular, is showing extraordinary business, with projections for the film to run at record levels there until the end of the second weekend. By the close of its second weekend, the film is expected to comfortably surpass the Rs. 600 crore mark.</p><p>Globally, Ramayana is also doing fantastic business, performing well in overseas territories and the southern states of India. The film's overall global target by the end of its theatrical run is estimated to be close to Rs. 2000 crore, signaling its widespread appeal and commercial success. The second weekend's trajectory will be crucial in determining if its final tally reaches Rs. 850 crore, Rs. 900 crore, or the Rs. 1000 crore club.</p><p>What to watch: Ramayana's performance in its second weekend.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures the box office estimates, context, and projections provided in the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-hindi-box-office-estimate-day-7-ranbir-kapoor-and-yash-starrer-clocks-rs-50-cr-plus-races-towards-rs-400-crore-club-in-7-days-flat/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-11-11/ramayana-nears-rs-400-crore-club-sets-new-week-one-record" data-title="Ramayana Nears Rs. 400 Crore Club, Sets New Week One Record"><b>Share:</b>
