       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana BJP Labels Congress Bharat Summit an 'Anti-Bharat' Event</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana BJP president N. Ramchander Rao has denounced the Congress’s Bharat Summit in Hyderabad as an ‘Anti-Bharat’ gathering. Rao alleged the event is a conspiratorial platform involving international entities and George Soros-backed groups intended to foster instability and weaken the government ahead of the 2029 general elections.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/telangana-bjp-labels-congress-bharat-summit-an-anti-bharat-e.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>He further claimed that foreign delegates are using the summit to project Rahul Gandhi internationally while utilizing Hyderabad as a base for unrest. Demanding transparency regarding funding, the BJP leader also criticized the Telangana government for past expenditures and urged a White Paper on state land transactions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The summary accurately captures the core allegations and the political context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/bjp-slams-congress-bharat-summit-calls-it-anti-bharat-event/article71689545.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
