       <h1>Telangana to Adopt 10+2 System from 2027-28</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Telangana</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#Policy</span> <span>#10+2 System</span></div>
       <p>The Telangana government has directed officials to replace the current Intermediate system with a 10+2 education structure starting from the 2027-28 academic year, according to The Times of India. The Chief Minister issued the directive to state officials regarding this significant structural change in the state’s education framework.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/telangana-to-adopt-102-system-from-2027-28.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The new 10+2 model will supersede the existing Intermediate system, marking a shift in how secondary and higher secondary education is organized in the region. Officials are now tasked with implementing the necessary administrative and logistical changes to ensure a smooth transition for students and institutions by the specified timeline.</p><p>What to watch: Official implementation guidelines and timelines for the 2027-28 rollout.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects the provided source summary regarding the educational policy change in Telangana.</p>
