     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>TTD official orders facility improvements at Tirumala</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Tirumala Tirupati Devasthanams (TTD) Additional Executive Officer Ch. Venkaiah Chowdary has directed officials to enhance cleanliness and amenities at accommodation complexes. During a review meeting, he ordered the establishment of a reception counter at the Annaprasadam complex to better serve pilgrims.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/ttd-official-orders-facility-improvements-at-tirumala.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Chowdary further mandated the installation of CCTV cameras and complaint boxes at luggage counters to improve safety. Officials were instructed to prioritize the Nandakam app, ensuring that technical issues reported by devotees are resolved within 24 hours. Additionally, staff must promote greater awareness regarding the conservation of water and electricity among visiting pilgrims.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the directives issued by the TTD official based on the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/ttd-additional-eo-directs-officials-to-improve-pilgrim-facilities/article71689712.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
