     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-11 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Victim's Daughter Challenges Minor's Bail in Cheranalloor Accident Case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bhadrakeerthi R.J. has filed a criminal review petition in the Kerala High Court challenging the November 5 bail granted to a minor involved in a fatal October 25 accident in Cheranalloor. Her father, Jayabalakrishnan, died after his two-wheeler was struck by a luxury car allegedly driven by the minor.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-11/victims-daughter-challenges-minors-bail-in-cheranalloor-acci.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The petition argues the children's court's decision was illegal and ignored the Juvenile Justice Act, 2015, which mandates bail denial if release defeats the ends of justice. The plea contends that releasing the minor in a high-fatality case involving gross vehicular recklessness undermines public confidence in the rule of law.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the legal challenge and the context of the accident, though it omits the minor's family background, which is acceptable for brevity.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/daughter-of-cheranalloor-accident-victim-files-review-petition-before-kerala-high-court/article71690911.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
